  "paragraph": 18,
  "text": "Without clever engineering, output tokens would cost twenty or fifty times more. Labs fight the memory wall by shrinking what crosses the HBM bus. Quantization trims weights down to eight or four bits. Grouped-Query Attention, or GQA, and Multi-Head Latent Attention, or MLA, compress the KV cache. And Mixture of Experts, or MoE, activates only a fraction of weights per token.",
